      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 Elsevier B.V. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "The novel and green procedure to synthesis of 3-substituted coumarins was performed through the Knoevenagel condensation between various salicylaldehydes and 1,3-dicarbonyl compounds by MgFe2O4 nanoparticles as an efficient catalyst under solvent-free condition using ultrasound irradiation. The nano catalyst was easily recovered by an external magnet and reused for several times without significant loss of its catalytic performance. Compare to the previous works, this progressive protocol have advantages such as simple workup, high yields of coumarins, solvent free condition, environmentally benign and short reaction times."
      },
